From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Register the clocks before enabling
 runtime PM

The clock framework enables runtime PM support for a clock when its
provider device already has runtime PM enabled at registration. Such a
clock takes a runtime PM reference on the provider while it is
prepared. qmp_combo_probe() registers the pipe and DP clocks after
enabling runtime PM, so they hold a reference on the PHY device whenever
they are prepared.

The USB pipe clock that the PHY consumes is a child of the PHY's own
pipe clock and is prepared from qmp_combo_com_init() to
qmp_combo_com_exit(), i.e. for as long as the PHY is initialised. The
PHY therefore keeps itself runtime active, and even when userspace
allows runtime PM through power/control it never runtime suspends and
never enters autonomous mode, so a device plugged into an idle port
cannot wake the controller through the PHY.

Register the clocks before runtime PM is enabled. None of these clocks
accesses PHY registers, so they do not need the PHY to be resumed.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 5f19447be79..e0323a6520b 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -5822,6 +5822,17 @@ static int qmp_combo_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_node_put;
 
+	/*
+	 * Register the clocks before enabling runtime PM. A clock registered
+	 * afterwards takes a runtime PM reference on this device while it is
+	 * prepared, and the pipe clock stays prepared as long as the PHY is
+	 * initialized, so the PHY could never runtime suspend and enter
+	 * autonomous mode. None of these clocks touches the PHY registers.
+	 */
+	ret = qmp_combo_register_clocks(qmp, usb_np, dp_np);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_node_put;
+
 	/*
 	 * Enable runtime PM before creating the PHYs, phy_create() only enables
 	 * it on the PHY devices if already enabled on the parent. Hold a usage
@@ -5838,10 +5849,6 @@ static int qmp_combo_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 */
 	pm_runtime_forbid(dev);
 
-	ret = qmp_combo_register_clocks(qmp, usb_np, dp_np);
-	if (ret)
-		goto err_pm_put;
-
 	qmp->usb_phy = devm_phy_create(dev, usb_np, &qmp_combo_usb_phy_ops);
 	if (IS_ERR(qmp->usb_phy)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(qmp->usb_phy);
-- 
